Description: Render presets that write a stereoscopic 3D video, marked
 A new group, Stereoscopic 3D, with H.264 and HEVC in MP4 and Matroska. Each writes
 the project's frames as they are, full side by side with the left eye first, and
 asks MLT's avformat consumer for stereo3d=side_by_side: the frame packing
 arrangement SEI (H.264 D.2.26, by libx264; H.265 D.3.16, by FFmpeg's
 hevc_metadata in the edition's MLT), Matroska's StereoMode 1 (RFC 9559,
 5.1.4.1.28.3) and MP4's st3d box, which FFmpeg's MP4 muxer writes only with
 strict=-1 (FF_COMPLIANCE_UNOFFICIAL). A project with no 3D clip, or whose frames
 the person declared packed another way, is refused with a message saying why,
 so a 2D video is never marked 3D.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-20

